     Question
To accommodate the backup agent tool's specifications, the system admin team at xFusionCorp Industries requires the creation of a user with a non-interactive shell. Here's your task:
1-Create a user named mark with a non-interactive shell on App Server 3.
Note: You can find the infrastructure details by clicking on the Details of all Users and Servers button on the top-right section of the page.

   Solution

1- Login into app server 3
    ssh banner@stapp03
2- Create the user with a non-interactive shell
    sudo useradd -s /sbin/nologin mark
Note:- -s /sbin/nologin → sets the shell to non-interactive (user cannot log in interactively).
- mark → username.
- Alternative: Some systems use /bin/false instead of /sbin/nologin. Both prevent interactive logins, but /sbin/nologin provides a clearer message.
3- Set a password only if required by policy
(Optional, since the shell is non-interactive):
    sudo passwd mark
4- Validate the user creation
 .Check user entry:
    getent passwd mark
 .Expected output
    mark:x:UID:GID::/home/mark:/sbin/nologin
 .Confirm login shell
    grep mark /etc/passwd 
